distinguished speakers and fellow  researchers a very warm greeting to one  and all  my name is shrigary krishnakumar i am a  research intern at pine biotech  i am here to talk about my journey to  bioinformatics through omics logic  training platform  i completed my undergraduate degree in  forensic science from amity university  noida india  after completing my undergraduate degree  i joined pentagram discovery which  focuses on zebrafish as a research model  for drug screening and drug efficacy  studies  as a research assistant i had the  opportunity to work on several disease  models including parkinson's  huntington's pancreatic tumor and  diabetes to name a few  as i continued to work on these projects  i started coming across several research  articles that talked about the  applications of machine learning and  data science in zebrafish models  especially in the field of neuroscience  i got fascinated as i started learning  more and i soon realized that i wish to  work at the intersection of biomedical  science and computer science  but before pursuing my higher studies in  this field there were few factors that  were important to consider  one is that before pursuing an expensive  master's degree i wanted to network with  the peers in this field to know more  about the opportunities and scope of  this field secondly i wanted to work on  a hands-on research project to get an  idea of what it is like to work in this  field and finally i've always admired  the mentor-mentee relationship and  throughout my learning experience i  wanted to receive guidance from an  expert who's already working in this  field  and the only program that was available  at the intersection of all these three  factors were the omex logic research  fellowship program and i got enrolled  the initial months of my program were  devoted to training and so far i have  completed the following courses on  introduction to bioinformatics genomics  transcriptomics our coding course 2  introduction to data science and project  on modelling cancer precision medicine  and apart from my coursework learning  i'm also working on my research project  that aims to conduct transcriptomic  profiling of chlamydia pneumonia  infected coronary artery endothelial  cells to study their role in the  progression of atherosclerosis in  coronary artery disease patients  and as an intern at pine biotech i am  also responsible for creating blogs and  as a part of my work i recently had the  opportunity to write a blog on best  online courses on bioinformatics and  after reviewing several of these courses  i grew to admire the uniqueness of the  courses and project opportunities  offered by the omics logic learning  platform  here are some of the key highlights of  the program from the from my perspective  as a student from non-bioinformatics  background  first of all the library of asynchronous  learning material on topics  ranging from genomics to metagenomics  that takes you from the beginner level  to the advanced level  secondly there are numerous sample  projects that are sourced from high  impact research publications in the  field of oncology biotechnology  neuroscience agriculture and infectious  diseases  the weekly research fellowship meetings  where you can share your queries  research project updates and receive  expert feedback on how to progress  further is also my favorite  there is also an active peer community  consisting of enthusiastic faculties  students and researchers who are  learning and working on the research  problems that they are curious about  and finally the omics logic and fine  biotech team has been extremely  supportive right from the start of the  program and helped me during every step  of the program  to conclude i wish to say whether you  are a student a researcher or even if  you wish to be part of the citizen  science to contribute to the scientific  community through the use of  bioinformatics i would highly recommend  you to join the omics project learning  platform  would like to take this opportunity to  thank mr eliabrotsky dr mohad mazumdar  dr raghvendran lakshmi narayan mr ali  kha ray and ms bash there for being the  constant source of support during the  every step of the program thank you
 

